Resolved for me! The problem is that the old ```TABLE_COLLATION``` value is left in the database. It was default for mysql 5.7 - ```utf8mb4_general_ci```, which is different from the default for mysql 8 - ```utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci```.
Executed a view query for all tables:
```
set foreign_key_checks=0;
...
alter table api_keys convert to character set utf8mb4 collate utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci;
...
set foreign_key_checks=1;
```
And the update was successful!

